# Secrets — never commit real settings, only the .template.json versions
#
# ⚠️ Ignoring is NOT the same as not syncing. If this workspace sits inside a
# cloud-synced folder (Google Drive / Dropbox / OneDrive / iCloud), that client
# replicates these files to every machine regardless of what git thinks — along
# with any absolute paths, permission modes, or MCP endpoints inside them.
# Machine-specific settings belong OUTSIDE the synced folder, in the user scope:
#   $env:USERPROFILE\.claude\settings.json   (Windows)
#   ~/.claude/settings.json                  (macOS / Linux)
# See AGENTS.md § Multi-Machine & Sync Safety.
.claude/settings.json
.claude/settings.local.json
.env
.env.*
*.pem
credentials.json
secrets.*
